/**
 * @defgroup KludGeo KludGeo — Kludge Effective-Material Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definition for configurable effective-material volumes
 *        (KLUD)
 *
 * @details
 * KludGeo (module name KludGeo) provides a generic mechanism for inserting
 * user-specified effective material volumes into the STAR simulation without
 * modifying any detector-specific geometry code.  It places up to ten
 * cylindrical disk or tube volumes (KTUB) along the z-axis, each with fully
 * configurable position, radii, half-length, and material properties (atomic
 * mass, atomic number, density).  The default material is aluminium
 * (A=27, Z=13, ρ=2.7 g/cm³).
 *
 * The module is intended for systematic studies, material scans of prototype
 * detectors, or situations where a detector's material budget is known but its
 * geometry is not yet implemented.  Its use in production simulation is
 * strongly discouraged.
 *
 * ## Operation
 *
 * The `KCFG_ntube` parameter controls how many KTUB volumes are created; it
 * defaults to 0 (no volumes placed).  When the KLUDon setup is active, the
 * user may set `ntube` and the KTUB array parameters at runtime via the
 * simulation job configuration.  The `runtime="True"` attribute on the KLUDon
 * setup enables this runtime override.
 *
 * Each placed KTUB uses konly="MANY" so it can overlap with other volumes.
 * The geometry and material are reported via AGML @c Info statements for
 * each tube placed.
 *
 * ## Setup configurations
 *
 * | Setup name | onoff | ntube | Description |
 * |------------|-------|-------|-------------|
 * | KLUDof     | off   | —     | No kludge volumes (default off) |
 * | KLUDon     | on    | 0     | Enabled; no volumes unless ntube set at runtime |
 *
 * ## KTUB parameter arrays (length 10)
 *
 * Default values (all aluminium, symmetric z):
 * - z:   {±1000, ±900, ±800, ±700, ±600} cm
 * - dz:  0.5 cm half-length each
 * - rmn: 5.0 cm inner radius each
 * - rmx: 255.0 cm outer radius each
 * - AA:  27, ZZ: 13, DD: 2.7 g/cm³
 *
 * ## Volume hierarchy
 * @code
 * KTUB  (TUBE — up to 10 instances placed in CAVE with konly=MANY)
 * @endcode
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @file KludGeo.xml
 * @brief Kludge effective-material geometry (KludGeo module).
 * Places up to 10 user-configured cylindrical material volumes in CAVE.
 * Default ntube = 0; material defaults to aluminium.
 * Author: Jason Webb (1 April 2018).
 */

